## PM Operating System

This workspace follows the PATI PM Operating System. Read before non-trivial work.

| Read this | When |
|---|---|
| `__PMOS_PATH__/pm-operating-system.md` | Any product work. Three phases, ten stages |
| `__PMOS_PATH__/product-development-framework.md` | Before a spec exists. Gates B1–B9 + the eight-plane trace |
| `__PMOS_PATH__/linear-collab.md` | Work is tracked in Linear, or a second person/agent is involved |
| `__PMOS_PATH__/triage-labels.md` | Assigning or reading a triage label |
| `Skills/meta/task-routing.md` | Choosing which skills to load |

### Two gates before any spec

**Gate 1 · Business (B1–B9)** — persona, today's workaround and its cost, the named
problem, which KPI moves, an existing backlog id, adoption hypothesis, the unused
signal, the smallest version, and what happens if we do not build it.

**Gate 2 · Connection (eight planes)** — business, process, modules (forward *and*
reverse), API, data, external, cross-cutting, knowledge.

Killing or parking at a gate is a **successful** outcome. Every deferred seam costs
a `TD-` or `BL-` id.

Skip rule: a genuine one-line bug may skip Gate 1. **Nothing skips Gate 2.**

### Evidence precedence

```text
runtime  >  commit  >  chat  >  none
```

Never collapse these. Code beats docs; runtime beats code. A disagreement is a
finding, not something to paper over.

- A green test run is not a deployment.
- A skipped required test did not pass.
- An interrupted external write stays `unknown`, not `failed` or `0 created`.
- Full verification runs **once, at the end**. Focused checks may run during work.

### Stop conditions

- Three failed fix attempts → pause and escalate. Do not keep trying.
- No free `BL-`/`TD-` id without a collision → do not mint the next free one.
- A dirty working tree is not yours to commit.
- Production impact → contain or roll back first, then diagnose.
- Never redeploy something you do not understand.

### Diagrams

Prefer `/archify` — it validates geometry, proves desktop containment in a real
browser, and reports SHA-256 receipts. `/architecture-diagram` is the fallback for
when shell or Node is unavailable; it has no automated proof, so say so when you use it.

Specs live in `__PMOS_PATH__/../canvas/`. Rendered output goes to
`Outputs/<Project>/`, never into a note folder.

### Shipped is not done

Adoption re-checks B6 (who opens this, how often) and B7 (how we learn nobody uses it)
**in the runtime**, not in the diff. An incident buys a structural ordering rule,
not a patch.
